@startuml path-exact-closure-occurrence
' ============================================================================
' The decision that verify_incremental_closure makes for one logical
' occurrence (task 11957; closure.rs:927-1210), and the final reachability
' check. Theory: formal/rocq/stack_safe_pda/theories/PathExactIncrementalClosure.v
'   BLUE   #1565C0  the walk: pop, authenticate, parse, push
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the overlay lookup, which the correction moves after the
'                   exact-certificate decision, and the note that explains it
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  acceptance: an inherited boundary, or the whole delta
'   RED    #C62828  refusals
'   GREY   #607D8B  checks that the correction leaves unchanged
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>One occurrence of the path-exact incremental closure walk</b>\nan occurrence is (reference r, expectation e, exact absolute path p)

start
:push the target manifest at the empty path; <<#BBDEFB>>
while (work remains?) is (yes)
  :pop (r, e, p); <<#BBDEFB>>
  if (e is a node or a content blob\nand a certificate names exactly\n(namespace(e), kind(e), p, r)?) then (yes)
    :stop at an inherited boundary:\nthe base owns this occurrence; <<#C8E6C9>>
  else (no)
    :look r up in the staging overlay; <<#FFE0B2>>
    if (r staged?) then (no)
      :refuse MissingObject(r); <<#FFCDD2>>
      stop
    else (yes)
      :authenticate r once per digest\n(declared length, digest),\ncheck for a cycle; <<#CFD8DC>>
      :parse r as e expects at p,\nvalidate the node context\nand the endpoint policy; <<#CFD8DC>>
      :record r as reached,\npush its content at p + prefix\nand each child at p + prefix + edge; <<#BBDEFB>>
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no)
if (every staged object reached?) then (yes)
  :accept the delta; <<#C8E6C9>>
else (no)
  :refuse: the transaction staged an\nobject outside the target delta closure; <<#FFCDD2>>
endif
stop

note right #FFF3E0
  <b>The defect</b> (J-037, Algorithm 3): the overlay was
  consulted first, and a certificate only for an object
  that was not staged. A node emitted at one path can be
  byte-identical to an untouched subtree certified at
  another; the old walk descended into that subtree there
  and refused a valid delta with MissingObject.
  ----
  <b>The correction</b> (J-251): the exact certificate is
  checked first. Outcomes differ only at a <i>coincident</i>
  occurrence, one that is certified and whose reference is
  also staged (verifiers_agree_without_coincidence).
end note
@enduml
